  (text_box "Description: Analog Front Ends - Channel A & B. Two matched signal chains conditioning BNC inputs (J6/J7) for the ADC. Each: 1 MΩ input (R61/R62) for ×10-probe compatibility, protection (1 kΩ series + SMAJ48CA TVS + BAV199-type clamp D10/D11 to ±5 V), an AD8066 unity-gain buffer, a summing/level-shift stage adding the DAC offset (DAC1_OUT1/OUT2 → vertical position) to center the bipolar signal in the 0-3.0 V ADC window, and a ~1.16 MHz Sallen-Key anti-alias filter (U15) into ADC12_INP3/INP4. Each op-amp is locally decoupled (4.7 µF + 100 nF per rail); runs on the clean ±5 V analog rails."
    (at 177.8 147.32 0) (size 104.14 15.24)
    (stroke (width 0) (type default))
    (fill (type color) (color 255 255 194 1))
    (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27) bold) (justify left top))
    (uuid b7f0cc2b-a049-4d3e-b94b-7c05e66623bc)
  )

